BT 1 0 0 1 8 102 Tm /F1 10 Tf 16 TL 1.208125 Tw (You have $5,000 in savings. You face three choices: Option A: Keep it in a savings account) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.374706 Tw (earning 2% per year ) Tj /F5 10 Tf 16 TL (\256) Tj /F1 10 Tf 16 TL ( $5,100 after one year Option B: Pay off a credit card charging 18%) Tj T* 0 Tw .213529 Tw (interest ) Tj /F5 10 Tf 16 TL (\256) Tj /F1 10 Tf 16 TL ( saves $900 in interest = equivalent to earning 18% Option C: Invest in an index fund) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.686875 Tw (with expected 10% return ) Tj /F5 10 Tf 16 TL (\256) Tj /F1 10 Tf 16 TL ( ~$5,500 after one year, but with risk This IS finance. You are) Tj T* 0 Tw .504167 Tw (raising \(your savings\), allocating \(choosing between options\), investing \(Options A and C\), and) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.568182 Tw (managing \(monitoring performance\). The 'right' answer depends on your risk tolerance, time) Tj T* 0 Tw (horizon, and other debts \227 exactly the kind of analysis finance teaches you to do.) Tj T* ET
